Title      : cpu: memory address with the operand forwarding select after the adder
Project    : fpga-mister (patch for N64_MiSTer 5725381)
Author     : Konstantin Schmidt (mr_pleasant@gmx.de)
Company    : OHRZ
Created    : 2026-10-31
Description:
  calcMemAddr (stage 3) adds the immediate to value1, the forwarding mux of
  resultData, writebackData and decodeValue1.  On the xc7z020 at 93.75 MHz
  the select (executeForwardValue1 and resultWriteEnable, fan-out ~90) in
  front of the 64-bit carry chain starts the CPU's worst paths: address ->
  TLB, COP0 BadVAddr/EntryHi, cache tag, executeMemAddress, stall (a
  build without it: 389 failing endpoints, -1.728 ns, most from
  resultWriteEnable).  cores/n64/cpu_addr_fwd.vhd adds the immediate to each
  source and selects the sum: the same value in every cycle, the select
  moves behind the adders.  Bench n64_cpu_addr_fwd_tb (against the original
  expression, 5 mutants).
--- a/rtl/cpu.vhd	2026-10-31 17:48:41.105688353 +0100
+++ b/rtl/cpu.vhd	2026-10-31 17:48:41.113442910 +0100
@@ -2087,7 +2087,19 @@
    value2_muxedSigned <= unsigned(resize(signed(decodeImmData), 64)) when (decodeUseImmidateValue2) else value2;
    calcResult_add     <= value1 + value2_muxedSigned;
    
-   calcMemAddr        <= value1 + unsigned(resize(signed(decodeImmData), 64));
+   -- fpga-mister: forwarding select after the adder (timing on the xc7z020, cores/n64/cpu_addr_fwd.vhd)
+   icpu_addr_fwd : entity work.n64_cpu_addr_fwd
+   port map
+   (
+      resultData             => resultData,
+      writebackData          => writebackData,
+      decodeValue1           => decodeValue1,
+      decodeImmData          => decodeImmData,
+      executeForwardValue1   => executeForwardValue1,
+      resultWriteEnable      => resultWriteEnable,
+      writebackForwardValue1 => writebackForwardValue1,
+      calcMemAddr            => calcMemAddr
+   );
    
    ---------------------- Shifter ------------------
    -- multiplex immidiate and register based shift amount, so both types can use the same shifters
